      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hey ・Wikked・, I 100% agree with this suggestion. Adding a built-in messaging feature for friends—especially one that supports text, images, or even short voice clips—would massively improve social interaction on VRChat. It’d be super helpful for coordination, sharing media, or just checking in with friends without needing to rely on third-party platforms like Discord.\n\nGroup messaging (with mute options) is also a great idea, especially for event planning or community worlds. Hope the devs take this into consideration—this could be a huge step toward making VRChat feel more like a connected, social hub. �",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-05-14T20:39:04.880Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I'd love to see an option that allows for sending messages to people on your friends list. Something that allows text, images, or even short voice messages. I think it would allow for more social interaction. Think of it like this, you open a friend's profile and there's a button to click that says \"message\" or something similar. It would be great for communication with friends who aren't in your insurance. Also if this could possibly be added to groups for group messages (with an option to mute of course).",
